delta variant has health officials on  alert for the uptick in covid cases  nevada reporting more than 100 confirmed  cases  christian costa is joining us in studio  to break down why this has become such a  problem  brian the delta variant is a mutation of  the kovitz strain and according to an  infectious disease expert at unlv  we can expect more variants like this  one in the coming years today we spoke  to brian lubis  an infectious disease expert at unlv  school of public health  he says the biggest difference between  this strain and other strains is what  it's basically it spreads more easily  there have been no reports of it causing  different diseases  deadlier or more hospitalizations  according to him it's all about the  person-to-person spread which of course  will lead to more transmission  in the community because it's so  contagious he says the only way to know  if you have the delta variant  is through a specialized test at the  state public health lab  a normal cova test will not tell you  what strain you have  he says it doesn't change how you are  treated but it's important for tracking  the variant  well we're going to continue to see  different variants popping up that's  just the way viruses spread  their copying mechanism isn't perfect so  there are changes that  build up over time and if one of those  variants spreads more easily than the  strain that's the dominant strain now  that one will basically out-compete it  and take over as the dominant strain so  we're seeing more and more delta-variant  cases  well the cdc and the southern nevada  health district are not modifying face  mask mandates like those in la county  they recommend everyone vaccinate  vaccinated or not to wear a mask  in large gatherings now he says people  should be more concerned the people who  should be more concerned are those who  have not been vaccinated because  basically they have no protection  so check out eightnewsnow.com to  schedule your vaccine christian casadas  8 news now
 

